# /etc/hunter/signatures — hunter's local antivirus database.
#
# Read at boot together with every file in /etc/hunter/signatures.d/ (where
# `hunterctl update-signatures` keeps the downloaded feeds). One signature per
# line; a line that does not parse is skipped by name, the rest still load:
#
#   hash:<sha256>:<Name>     the SHA-256 of a whole known-bad file
#   bytes:<hex>:<Name>       a byte pattern inside one; `??` matches any byte.
#                            At least 4 fixed bytes, starting with a fixed one.
#
# Signatures can also be added to a running system, never removed:
#   echo 'signature bytes:deadbeef:Example' > /proc/hunter
#
# The EICAR test file: harmless, and what every antivirus is tested with.
# `printf '%s' 'X5O!P%@AP[4\PZX54(P^)7CC)7}$EICAR-STANDARD-ANTIVIRUS-TEST-FILE!$H+H*' > /tmp/eicar.com`
# then `hunterctl scan /tmp` should report it.
